From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: serial: option: reset_resume callback for WWAN devices

The PinePhone's USB host controller (ehci-platform) is reset and powered
down in suspend, so on resume the modem (EG25-G) gets a USB reset (USB
persist keeps the device). option has no reset_resume, so usb-serial
answers -EOPNOTSUPP and the USB core unbinds and binds its interfaces
again: the AT ports are removed and created again, the one still open
coming back under another number (ttyUSB2, then ttyUSB3), and what the
modem said meanwhile (an incoming call's RING) is lost. The modem itself
did not restart, so resuming as after a plain suspend is enough.

The same change as postmarketOS's linux-postmarketos-allwinner
0014-usb-serial-option-add-reset-resume-callback-for-WWAN.patch
(Thomas Thorne, 2022, from the Quectel community patches); not in
mainline.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/serial/option.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/serial/option.c
@@ -2580,6 +2580,7 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
 	.suspend           = usb_wwan_suspend,
 	.resume            = usb_wwan_resume,
+	.reset_resume      = usb_wwan_resume,
 #endif
 };
